examples.solution_text:
The complement of ‘at least one win’ is ‘no wins’. The probabilities of not winning are $0.3$ and $0.5$.
The tree uses $W$ for wins and $N$ for does not win. The blue path represents no wins.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},line width=0.5pt]
\definecolor{complementBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (2.8,1.5);
\coordinate (B) at (2.8,-1.5);
\coordinate (C) at (5.6,2.3);
\coordinate (D) at (5.6,0.7);
\coordinate (E) at (5.6,-0.7);
\coordinate (F) at (5.6,-2.3);
\draw (O)--(A);
\draw[complementBlue,thick] (O)--(B);
\draw (A)--(C);
\draw (A)--(D);
\draw (B)--(E);
\draw[complementBlue,thick] (B)--(F);
\path (O)--(A) node[midway,above,fill=white] {$0.7$};
\path (O)--(B) node[midway,below,fill=white] {$0.3$};
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,above,fill=white] {$0.5$};
\path (A)--(D) node[midway,below,fill=white] {$0.5$};
\path (B)--(E) node[midway,above,fill=white] {$0.5$};
\path (B)--(F) node[midway,below,fill=white] {$0.5$};
\path (A) node[fill=white] {$W$};
\path (B) node[fill=white] {$N$};
\path (C) node[right] {$W\quad WW$};
\path (D) node[right] {$N\quad WN$};
\path (E) node[right] {$W\quad NW$};
\path (F) node[right] {$N\quad NN$};
\path (2.8,3) node {Race 1};
\path (5.6,3) node {Race 2};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}P(\text{no wins})&=0.3\times0.5\\&=0.15\end{aligned}$
$\begin{aligned}P(\text{at least one win})&=1-0.15\\&=0.85\end{aligned}$
